## 6. Methodology and limitations

The findings derive from a point-in-time automated scan of the publicly accessible pages of {{controller.domain}} performed on {{scanDate}}{{#if scanMeta.scanner}} using {{scanMeta.scanner}}{{#if scanMeta.browser}} ({{scanMeta.browser}}){{/if}}{{/if}}. The scan loads the site in a clean browser session and records network requests, cookies, browser storage, and consent-banner behaviour before any consent interaction, after accepting consent, and after rejecting consent where those options were available.

Limitations the authority should be aware of:

- The observations reflect the site's behaviour at the time of the scan; the site may behave differently now.
- The scan covers publicly accessible pages only — no logged-in areas, checkout flows, or native applications.
- Server-side processing (including server-to-server data sharing) is not observable from the browser and is not covered by these findings.
- An automated scan may not trigger all tracking present on the site; the findings are a lower bound on the observed processing, not an exhaustive inventory.

